message.content:
{
  "action": "check_meters",
  "note": "The tin is in my tray. Sealed. That's enough. I'm not going to slide Phil a weather card like I'm dodging, and I'm not going to open the desk phone and say his name is Mercury, that my brother's voice is on that tape, that the last thing on the outtake is *your mic is still on* and I still can't tell if it was a warning or a lullaby. That's the archive. That's mine. 80 seconds to the wire handoff and the acoustic window is clear and the line meter is the only thing I need right now. I keep the handoff reserved. I watch the needle. I let the lamp count down. Phil can have his ordinary copy card later, or he can not. The distinctive broadcast is the one I control, and right now controlling means: hands on the faders, eyes on the meter, the tin in the tray, the drawer combination 4042 in my head where it's always been. I don't owe anyone the origin. Not at 80 seconds. Not to Phil. Not to the wire. I check the meters and I keep the handoff mine."
}
